Guide for developing UI components in WhatNext following established patterns, design philosophy, and common pitfalls. The UI is built with React 19, Tailwind CSS v4, and follows an Obsidian-inspired, developer-focused aesthetic.
Local-First Indicators: UI constantly reinforces local-first architecture
Information Density: Compact yet readable, maximizing screen real estate
Visual Hierarchy: Clear parent/child relationships via indentation and borders
Developer-Focused: Tools and workflows prominently featured
Progressive Disclosure: Collapse sections to focus, expand for detail
Color Palette:
Primary Blue (#3B82F6): Active states, highlights
Purple Accent (#9333EA): Brand gradient, special features
Gray Scale: Dark sidebar (900), subtle borders (800), muted text (400-600)
Semantic Colors: Green: Online/active status
Orange: Development/in-progress
Gray: Coming soon/inactive Typography:
Section headers: Uppercase, tracked, small (text-xs)
Nav items: Normal case, medium (text-sm)
Badges: Tiny, bold (text-[10px])
Clear size hierarchy for readability
Example: Sidebar with collapsible sectionsconst [expandedSections, setExpandedSections] = useState&lt;Set&lt;string&gt;&gt;( new Set(['workspace', 'p2p-network', 'development'])
); const toggleSection = (sectionId: string) =&gt; { setExpandedSections(prev =&gt; { const next = new Set(prev); if (next.has(sectionId)) { next.delete(sectionId); } else { next.add(sectionId); } return next; });
}; // Section header
&lt;button onClick={() =&gt; toggleSection('workspace')} className="flex items-center justify-between w-full px-3 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-300"
&gt; &lt;span&gt;WORKSPACE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;ChevronIcon className={expandedSections.has('workspace') ? 'rotate-90' : ''} /&gt;
&lt;/button&gt; // Child items (only if expanded)
{expandedSections.has('workspace') &amp;&amp; ( &lt;div className="space-y-1"&gt; {/* Nav items */} &lt;/div&gt;
)}
Key Features:
Set-based state for O(1) lookup
Smooth rotation animation on chevron
Clear visual hierarchy with indentation
Three badge types:// "Soon" badge (gray)
&lt;span className="text-[10px] font-bold px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-gray-700 text-gray-400 rounded"&gt; Soon
&lt;/span&gt; // "Dev" badge (orange)
&lt;span className="text-[10px] font-bold px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-orange-500/20 text-orange-400 rounded"&gt; Dev
&lt;/span&gt; // "Issue #X" badge (blue)
&lt;span className="text-[10px] font-bold px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-blue-500/20 text-blue-400 rounded"&gt; #4
&lt;/span&gt;
Usage:
Soon: Planned features not yet implemented
Dev: Development/debug tools
Issue X: Linked to GitHub issue tracking
